{"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"],"anchor":"Sorted-sets","title":"Sorted sets","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in a splay tree: a binary search tree that rotates each element it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accesses, inserts or removes up to the root (Sleator and Tarjan, 1985).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SplayTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A splay tree keeps no balance information. Any sequence of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" insertions, removals and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accesses on "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" elements costs O(("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in all, so each takes O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"amortized, and recently or frequently accessed elements stay near the root: accessing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements in ascending order costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in all. Reads ("},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the bounds, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscripts and iteration) leave the tree as it is, so they keep the value semantics and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API of the other sorted sets, and take time proportional to the element’s depth, which a run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of ascending insertions can make "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/access(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to look an element up and splay it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root","recent.contains(25)           \/\/ false, and the tree is unchanged","let parts = recent.split(at: 30)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [10, 20]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [30, 40, 50]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array: "},{"code":"tree[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/splaytree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:17BinarySearchTrees9SplayTreeV","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SplayTree","modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SplayTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree.swift#L28"},"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/Split"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/init()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/B